What the fork changes: the extension, hook and option-merging machinery
is gone (the option set is fixed at marked's defaults), every grammar
regex is compiled once at module load, the block and inline scanners
only run the tokenizers whose opening character is present, and a few
masking and scanning passes are skipped when their trigger characters
do not occur. No parsing rule changes: for every input, parse(markdown)
returns the same HTML string as marked 18.1.3's marked.parse(markdown)
with default options.
